    {
      "id": "50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "person_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "kind": "pdf",
      "title": "Discharge summary",
      "storage_path": "demo/01-discharge-summary.pdf",
      "transcript": "BRISTOL ROYAL INFIRMARY. Department of Cardiology, Ward 8B. DISCHARGE SUMMARY. Patient: Margaret ELLIS. DOB 14/03/1944. Admitted: 21/06/2026. Discharged: 25/06/2026. Consultant: Dr A. Okafor. DIAGNOSIS: 1. Decompensated heart failure (HFrEF) 2. Chronic kidney disease stage 3b 3. Type 2 diabetes mellitus. CLINICAL COURSE: Renal function deteriorated during admission (creatinine rose from 118 to 164 umol/L) and diuretic therapy was adjusted accordingly. MEDICATION CHANGES ON DISCHARGE: Bisoprolol 2.5mg once daily — CONTINUE. Furosemide 40mg — STOPPED prior to discharge due to worsening renal function. Do not restart without review. Dapagliflozin 10mg once daily — NEW, started 23/06/2026. Metformin 500mg twice daily — CONTINUE. ACTIONS FOR PRIMARY CARE: GP to review renal function and diuretic requirement within 7 days of discharge. Daily weights. Contact GP if weight rises more than 2kg over 3 days. FOLLOW-UP: Heart failure specialist nurse to contact within 2 weeks. Cardiology outpatient review in 3 months.",
      "transcript_confidence": 0.98,
      "author_member_id": null,
      "created_at": "2026-07-20T09:12:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "person_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "kind": "image",
      "title": "Repeat prescription",
      "storage_path": "demo/02-repeat-prescription.jpg",
      "transcript": "ELMFIELD SURGERY. REPEAT PRESCRIPTION — PATIENT COPY. Mrs Margaret ELLIS. DOB 14/03/1944. Printed: 03/07/2026. Current repeat items: 1. Bisoprolol 2.5mg tablets 28 days. 2. Furosemide 40mg tablets 28 days. 3. Metformin 500mg tablets 56 days. 4. Atorvastatin 20mg tablets 28 days. 5. Amitriptyline 10mg tablets nocte 28 days. 6. Colecalciferol 800iu capsules 28 days. Last issued: 03/07/2026. Next review: not recorded.",
      "transcript_confidence": 0.81,
      "author_member_id": null,
      "created_at": "2026-07-20T09:14:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "person_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "kind": "pdf",
      "title": "Cardiology clinic letter",
      "storage_path": "demo/03-cardiology-letter.pdf",
      "transcript": "BRISTOL ROYAL INFIRMARY. Department of Cardiology. 12 March 2026. Dear Dr Mensah, I reviewed Mrs Ellis in the heart failure clinic today. She remains stable on her current regimen. Exercise tolerance is approximately 100 metres on the flat before stopping for breath. Echocardiography today shows left ventricular ejection fraction of 40%, with moderate mitral regurgitation. Renal function is stable with creatinine 118 umol/L, eGFR 42. Please continue furosemide 40mg daily and bisoprolol 2.5mg daily. I would be grateful if you would review her in six months. Yours sincerely, Dr A. Okafor, Consultant Cardiologist.",
      "transcript_confidence": 0.97,
      "author_member_id": null,
      "created_at": "2026-07-20T09:15:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "person_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "kind": "juno_conversation",
      "title": "Margaret's Juno history",
      "storage_path": "demo/04-juno-history.json",
      "transcript": "18 June 2026, evening: Very puffy round the ankles again today. Had to stop twice coming back from the shop. Slept sitting up. 26 June 2026, morning: Home from hospital yesterday. They were very good. Lots of new tablets and I'm not sure I've got them straight. 01 July 2026, evening: Breathing better than it was. Ankles still a bit puffy at night. 03 July 2026, evening: Still taking my water tablet at bedtime like always. Sarah asked about it on the phone. 09 July 2026, morning: Bit wobbly on the stairs this morning. Held on to the rail. Didn't tell Sarah, she worries. 16 July 2026, evening: Weight up a bit this week I think. The scales are in the bathroom and I don't always remember.",
      "transcript_confidence": 1.0,
      "author_member_id": null,
      "created_at": "2026-07-20T09:16:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "60000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "person_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Care log extract",
      "storage_path": "demo/documents/05-care-log.md",
      "transcript": "ELMFIELD HOME CARE — DAILY VISIT LOG Client: M. Ellis, 14 Elmfield Road Week commencing: 06/07/2026 Mon 06/07  0800  Assisted with washing and dressing. Prompted morning medication. Breakfast prepared. Settled. 1900  Evening call. Prompted medication. No concerns. Tue 07/07  0800  Assisted wash/dress. Prompted meds. Client reports poor night. Ankles swollen. 1900  Evening call. Prompted meds. Settled overnight, no incidents reported. Wed 08/07  0800  Assisted wash/dress. Hoist used for transfer to chair — client unsteady this morning. Prompted meds. 1900  PRN lorazepam 0.5mg administered at 2130 for agitation. Settled overnight, no incidents. Thu 09/07  0800  Assisted wash/dress. Prompted meds. Client mentioned feeling wobbly on stairs. 1900  Evening call. Prompted meds. Slept well, no concerns. Fri 10/07  0800  Assisted wash/dress. Prompted meds. Two-hourly repositioning continued per care plan. 1900  PRN lorazepam 0.5mg administered 2200. Settled. Sat 11/07  0800  Daughter staying for the weekend and covering personal care herself; carer attended for a welfare check only. Good day, no concerns, client in good spirits. 1900  Evening call. All well. Carer signature: J. Adeyemi",
      "transcript_confidence": 0.9,
      "author_member_id": null,
      "created_at": "2026-07-11T09:00:00Z"
    }
  ],

